# service centre receives an average of 4 customers every 10 minutes. The number of 
customer arrivals follows a Poisson distribution. 
Write a Python program to calculate the probability that exactly 6 customers arrive in a 10
minute interval, and to plot the probability mass function for customer arrivals from 0 to 12.





from scipy.stats import poisson
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

x = range(13)
print("P(X=6):", poisson.pmf(6,4))
plt.bar(x, poisson.pmf(x,4))
plt.show()
